company focused on building open-source developer tooling in Rust. The team has been active in the Cardano ecosystem since 2021, maintaining a portfolio of interconnected tools that serve as foundational infrastructure for Rust-based development on Cardano.\n\nTxPipe has received funding through multiple Cardano ecosystem programs, including Project Catalyst (Funds 9 through 14) for various tooling initiatives, and Intersect's budget process for ongoing maintenance of Pallas, Dolos, and UTxO RPC. All contracts are on track, with milestones being…\n# Criterion to evaluate\n**Output is open source**\nCode, docs, or data are released under an open licence.\n\nIs the code, documentation, or data being produced released under an open licence? Open source means anyone can read, fork, audit, and reuse the work — so the value the treasury is paying for stays available to the whole ecosystem forever, not locked inside one team. Closed-source deliverables die when the team moves on.\n# What I need from you\n1. Verdict: YES / NO / UNCLEAR — does this proposal meet the "])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"criterion?\n2. Confidence: LOW / MEDIUM / HIGH\n3. A short rationale (3–6 sentences) citing sources you actually checked (GitHub repos, Catalyst project pages, X/Twitter accounts, articles). Be honest if the public info is thin or the proposer's track-record claims need independent verification.\nPlease err on the side of \"UNCLEAR\" with expl…2a:[\"$\",\"tr\",\"open-source\",{\"className\":\"border-b border-[color:var(--border)] align-top last:border-0\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"td\",null,{\"className\":\"px-4 py-3 pr-2\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"flex items-baseline font-medium\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"children\":\"Output is open source\"}],[\"$\",\"$L22\",null,{\"label\":\"Output is open source\",\"body\":\"Is the code, documentation, or data being produced released under an open licence? Open source means anyone can read, fork, a