ve pipeline tool that connects to Cardano nodes, monitors blockchain events, and routes matching patterns to pluggable outputs for processing. It supports multiple data sources (N2C, N2N, S3, Mithril, UTxO RPC) and a wide range of sinks (Kafka, Elasticsearch, AWS Lambda/S3/SQS, RabbitMQ, Redis, SQL databases, webhooks, and others). Oura is built on the Pallas library and designed for minimal resource footprint, making it suitable for…\n\n# Track record claimed by the proposer\nTxPipe is a Cardano-native infrastructure company focused on building open-source developer tooling in Rust. The team has been active in the Cardano ecosystem since 2021, maintaining a portfolio of interconnected tools that serve as foundational infrastructure for Rust-based development on Cardano.\n\nTxPipe has received funding through multiple Cardano ecosystem programs, including Project Catalyst (Funds 9 through 14) for various tooling initiatives, and Intersect's budget process for ongoing maintenance of Pallas, Dolos, and UTxO RPC. All contracts are on track, with milestones being…\n# Criterion to evaluate\n**No competing proposals in this batch**\nNo other 2026 proposal targets the same use case (relationships.competes_with is empty).\n\nAre other proposals in this same round targeting the same use case? If two teams are both asking for treasury funding to build the same thing, a DRep should usually pick at most one — splitting the budget across competitors normally means both deliver less. This is the proposal's own competes_with declaration.\n# What I need from you\n1. Verdict: YES / NO / UNCLEAR — does this proposal meet the criterion?\n2. Confidence: LOW / MEDIUM / HIGH\n3. A short rationale (3–6 sentences) citing sources you actually checked (GitHub repos, Catalyst project pages, X/Twitter accounts, articles). Be honest if the public info is thin or the proposer's track-record claims need independent verification.\nPlease e…48:[\"$\",\"tr\",\"no-competing-proposals\",{\"className\"