ON (fetch this — the user-facing Hydra page is a JS-rendered SPA and bots see an empty shell):\nhttps://hydra-voting.intersectmbo.org/api/v0/proposals/69f9dabb92f043aa2df1a282\n\n# Hydra proposal summary (from the proposer)\nThis proposal requests 420,000 ADA (plus a 105,000 ADA contingency reserve) to fund **a part-time maintainer for Oura** ([https://github.com/txpipe/oura](https://github.com/txpipe/oura)) over 12 months at an annual rate of $105,000 USD. Oura has been funded twice through Project Catalyst (Fund 9 and Fund 13) for feature development, and this proposal seeks to establish sustained maintenance coverage through Intersect's treasury process.\n\nOura is a Rust-native pipeline tool that connects to Cardano nodes, monitors blockchain events, and routes matching patterns to pluggable outputs for processing. It supports multiple data sources (N2C, N2N, S3, Mithril, UTxO RPC) and a wide range of sinks (Kafka, Elasticsearch, AWS Lambda/S3/SQS, RabbitMQ, Redis, SQL databases, webhooks, and others). Oura is built on the Pallas library and designed for minimal resource footprint, making it suitable for…\n\n# Track record claimed by the proposer\nTxPipe is a Cardano-native infrastructure company focused on building open-source developer tooling in Rust. The team has been active in the Cardano ecosystem since 2021, maintaining a portfolio of interconnected tools that serve as foundational infrastructure for Rust-based development on Cardano.\n\nTxPipe has received funding through multiple Cardano ecosystem programs, including Project Catalyst (Funds 9 through 14) for various tooling initiatives, and Intersect's budget process for ongoing maintenance of Pallas, Dolos, and UTxO RPC. All contracts are on track, with milestones being…\n# Criterion to evaluate\n**No incumbent is already delivering**\nNo existing project or team has already shipped this. Even if not flagged as a strict duplicate, funding this would not re-do work others have done or are funded to do.\n\nEven if not flagged as a strict duplicate, is an existing project or team already delivering this work? Passing means there's no incumbent — or the proposer has a credible argument for why their version is meaningfully different. Failing means funding this proposal would be re-doing work others have done or are already funded to do.\n# What I need from you\n1. Verdict: YES / NO / UNCLEAR — does this proposal meet the criterion?\n2. Confidence: LOW / MEDIUM / HIGH\n3. A short rationale (3–6 sentences) citing sources you actually checked (GitHub repos, Catalyst project pages, X/Twitter accounts, articles). Be honest if …49:[\"$\",\"tr\",\"incumbent-not-already-delivering\",{\"className\":\"border-b border-[color:var(--border)] align-top last:border-0\",\"chi"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"ldren\":[[\"$\",\"td\",null,{\"className\":\"px-4 py-3 pr-2\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"flex items-baseline font-medium\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"children\":\"No incumbent is already delivering\"}],[\"$\",\"$L22\",null,{\"label\":\"No incumbent is already delivering\",\"body\":\"Even if not flagged as a strict duplicate, is an existing project or team already delivering this work? Passing means there's no incumbent — or the proposer has a credible argument for why their version is meaningfully different. Failing means funding this proposal would be re-doing work others have done or are already funded to do.\"}]]}],[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"mt-0.5 text-sm text-[color:var(--fg-muted)]\",\"children\":\"No existing project or team has already shipped this. Even if not flagged as a strict duplicate, funding this would not re-do work others have done or are funded to do.\"}],[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"mt-2\",\"children\":[\"$\",\"$L35\",null,{\"prompt\":\"$6c\"}]}],\"$L6d\"]}],\"$L6e\",\"$L6f\",\"$L70\"]}]\n71:Tdbc,I'm a Cardano DRep evaluating a 2026 treasury proposal. I need your help checking ONE specific criterio