t supports multiple data sources (N2C, N2N, S3, Mithril, UTxO RPC) and a wide range of sinks (Kafka, Elasticsearch, AWS Lambda/S3/SQS, RabbitMQ, Redis, SQL databases, webhooks, and others). Oura is built on the Pallas library and designed for minimal resource footprint, making it suitable for…\n\n# Track record claimed by the proposer\nTxPipe is a Cardano-native infrastructure company focused on building open-source developer tooling in Rust. The team has been active in the Cardano ecosystem since 2021, maintaining a portfolio of interconnected tools that serve as foundational infrastructure for Rust-based development on Cardano.\n\nTxPipe has received funding through multiple Cardano ecosystem programs, including Project Catalyst (Funds 9 through 14) for various tooling initiatives, and Intersect's budget process for ongoing maintenance of Pallas, Dolos, and UTxO RPC. All contracts are on track, with milestones being…\n# Criterion to evaluate\n**USD peg is not aggressive**\nPeg is conservative or neutral vs market — not requesting more ADA than spot would imply.\n\nProposals often denominate in USD at a chosen ADA price. If that peg is significantly below current market, the proposer is asking for more ADA than the same USD cost would actually require — an implicit overage. Conservative (at or above market) and neutral (within 5%) pegs are fine; aggressive pegs (more than 5% below market) are flagged.\n# What I need from you\n1. Verdict: YES / NO / UNCLEAR — does this proposal meet the criterion?\n2. Confidence: LOW / MEDIUM / HIGH\n3. A short rationale (3–6 sentences) citing sources you actually checked (GitHub repos, Catalyst project pages, X/Twitter accounts, articles). Be honest if the public info is thin or the proposer's track-record claims need independent v…51:[\"$\",\"tr\",\"usd-peg-not-aggressive\",{\"className\":\"border-b border-[color:var(--border)] align-top last:border-0\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"td\",null,{\"className\":\"px-4 py-3 pr-2\",\"children\