ding through multiple Cardano ecosystem programs, including Project Catalyst (Funds 9 through 14) for various tooling initiatives, and Intersect's budget process for ongoing maintenance of Pallas, Dolos, and UTxO RPC. All contracts are on track, with milestones being…\n# Criterion to evaluate\n**Has a treasury return clause**\nSurplus/unspent/revenue-share mechanism returns value to treasury.\n\nIs there a mechanism for unspent ADA, price-appreciation surplus, or revenue share to flow back to the treasury? Without one, every ADA the treasury sends is gone. With one, the proposer's incentives stay aligned: if they spend less than budgeted, or ADA goes up, the treasury gets some back.\n# What I need from you\n1. Verdict: YES / NO / UNCLEAR — does this proposal meet the criterion?\n2. Confidence: LOW / MEDIUM / HIGH\n3. A short rationale (3–6 sentences) citing sources you actually checked (GitHub repos, Catalyst project pages, X/Twitter accounts, articles). Be honest if the public info is thin or the proposer's track-record claims need independent verification.\nPlease err on the side of \"UNCLEAR\" with explanation rath…53:[\"$\",\"tr\",\"treasury-return-clause\",{\"className\":\"border-b border-[color:var(--border)] align-top last:border-0\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"td\",null,{\"className\":\"px-4 py-3 pr-2\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"flex items-baseline font-medium\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"children\":\"Has a treasury return clause\"}],[\"$\",\"$L22\",null,{\"label\":\"Has a treasury return clause\",\"body\":\"Is there a mechanism for unspent ADA, price-appreciation surplus, or revenue share to flow back to the treasury? Without one, every ADA the treasury sends is gone. With one, the proposer's incentives stay aligned: if they spend less than budgeted, or ADA goes up, the treasury gets some back.\"}]]}],[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"mt-0.5 text-sm text-[color:var(--fg-muted)]\",\"children\":\"Surplus/unspent/revenue-share