es, monitors blockchain events, and routes matching patterns to pluggable outputs for…\n\nFull proposal JSON (fetch this — the user-facing Hydra page is a JS-rendered SPA and bots see an empty shell):\nhttps://hydra-voting.intersectmbo.org/api/v0/proposals/69f9dabb92f043aa2df1a282\n\n# Hydra proposal summary (from the proposer)\nThis proposal requests 420,000 ADA (plus a 105,000 ADA contingency reserve) to fund **a part-time maintainer for Oura** ([https://github.com/txpipe/oura](https://github.com/txpipe/oura)) over 12 months at an annual rate of $105,000 USD. Oura has been funded twice through Project Catalyst (Fund 9 and Fund 13) for feature development, and this proposal seeks to establish sustained maintenance coverage through Intersect's treasury process.\n\nOura is a Rust-native pipeline tool that connects to Cardano nodes, monitors blockchain events, and routes matching patterns to pluggable outputs for processing. It supports multiple data sources (N2C, N2N, S3, Mithril, UTxO RPC) and a wide range of sinks (Kafka, Elasticsearch, AWS Lambda/S3/SQS, RabbitMQ, Redis, SQL databases, webhooks, and others). Oura is built on the Pallas library and designed for minimal resource footprint, making it suitable for…\n\n# Track record claimed by the proposer\nTxPipe is a Cardano-native infrastructure company focused on building open-source developer tooling in Rust. The team has been active in the Cardano ecosystem since 2021, maintaining a portfolio of interconnected tools that serve as foundational infrastructure for Rust-based development on Cardano.\n\nTxPipe has received funding through multiple Cardano ecosystem programs, including Project Catalyst (Funds 9 through 14) for various tooling initiatives, and Intersect's budget process for ongoing maintenance of Pallas, Dolos, and UTxO RPC. All contracts are on track, with milestones being…\n# Criterion to evaluate\n**Measurable on-chain KPIs**\nProposal commits to specific, verifiable on-chain outcomes -- transactions, unique wallets, mainnet deployments, TVL -- not just GitHub commits or off-chain deliverables.\n\nJudgment call: does the proposal commit to specific on-chain KPIs that anyone can verify directly from the chain? Strong looks like 'X mainnet transactions per month, Y unique wallets, Z dApps integrated, all queryable via blockfrost or db-sync'. Weak looks like 'increase Cardano adoption', 'community growth', 'GitHub stars', or any metric the proposer themselves controls. On-chain metrics are tamper-proof and let the community measure delivery against the actual ledger, not th"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"e proposer's self-reported numbers.\n# What I need from you\n1. Verdict: YES / NO / UNCLEAR — does this proposal meet the criterion?\n2. Confidence: L…59:[\"$\",\"tr\",\"measurable-onchain-kpis\",{\"className\":\"border-b border-[color:var(--border)] align-top last:border-0\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"td\",null,{\"className\":\"px-4 py-3 pr-2\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"flex items-baseline font-medium\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"children\":\"Measurable on-chain KPIs\"}],[\"$\",\"$L22\",null,{\"label\":\"Measurable on-chain KPIs\",\"body\":\"Judgment call: does the proposal commit to specific on-chain KPIs that anyone can verify directly from the chain? Strong looks like 'X mainnet transactions per month, Y unique wallets, Z dApps integrated, all queryable via blockfrost or db-sync'. Weak looks like 'increase Cardano adoption', 'community growth', 'GitHub stars', or any metric the proposer themselves controls. On-chain metrics are tamper-proof and let the community measure delivery against the actual ledger, not the proposer's self-reported numbers.\"}]]}],[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"mt-0.5 text-sm text-[color:var(--fg-muted)]\",\"children\":\"Proposal commits to specific, verifiable on-chain outcomes -- transactions, unique wallets, mainnet deployments, TVL -- not just GitHub commits or off-chain deliverables.