rch, AWS Lambda/S3/SQS, RabbitMQ, Redis, SQL databases, webhooks, and others). Oura is built on the Pallas library and designed for minimal resource footprint, making it suitable for…\n\n# Track record claimed by the proposer\nTxPipe is a Cardano-native infrastructure company focused on building open-source developer tooling in Rust. The team has been active in the Cardano ecosystem since 2021, maintaining a portfolio of interconnected tools that serve as foundational infrastructure for Rust-based development on Cardano.\n\nTxPipe has received funding through multiple Cardano ecosystem programs, including Project Catalyst (Funds 9 through 14) for various tooling initiatives, and Intersect's budget process for ongoing maintenance of Pallas, Dolos, and UTxO RPC. All contracts are on track, with milestones being…\n#"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1," Criterion to evaluate\n**Milestone payments disclosed**\nPayment is tied to itemised milestones, not lump sum.\n\nAre payments tied to delivery milestones, or is this lump-sum upfront? Milestone payments mean the treasury releases funds as work lands. Lump-sum upfront pays in full before anything is delivered — much less leverage if the team underdelivers.\n# What I need from you\n1. Verdict: YES / NO / UNCLEAR — does this proposal meet the criterion?\n2. Confidence: LOW / MEDIUM / HIGH\n3. A short rationale (3–6 sentences) citing sources you actually checked (GitHub repos, Catalyst project pages, X/Twitter accounts, articles). Be honest if the public info is thin or the proposer's track-record claims need independent verification.\nPlease err on the side of \"UNCLEAR\" with explanation rather than confident-but-wrong.5a:[\"$\",\"tr\",\"milestone-payments-disclosed\",{\"className\":\"border-b border-[color:var(--border)] align-top last:border-0\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"td\",null,{\"className\":\"px-4 py-3 pr-2\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"flex items-baseline font-medium\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"children\":\"Milestone payments disclosed\"}],[\"$\",\"$L22\",null,{\"label\":\"Milestone payments disclosed\",\"body\":\"Are payments tied to delivery milestones, or is this lump-sum upfront? Milestone payments mean the treasury releases funds as work lands. Lump-sum upfront pays in full before anything is delivered — much less leverage if the team underdelivers.\"}]]}],[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"mt-0.5 text-sm text-[color:var(--fg-muted)]\",\"children\":\"Payment is tied to itemised milestones, not lump sum.\"}],[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"mt-2\",\"children\":[\"$\",\"$L35\",null,{\"prompt\":\"$8f\"}]}],\"$L90\"]}],\"$L91\",\"$L92\",\"$L93\"]}]\n94:Tdac,I'm a Cardano DRep evaluating a 2026 treasury proposal. I need your help checking ONE specific criterion against this proposal. Please research the team and project before answering.\n# Proposal\nTitle: Oura by TxPipe: Maintaining Cardano's Event Pipeline\nProposer: TxPipe\nAbstract: This proposal requests 420,000 ADA (plus a 105,000 ADA contingency reserve) to fund **a part-time maintainer for Oura** ([https://github.com/txpipe/oura](https://github.com/txpipe/oura)) over 12 months at an annual rate of $105,000 USD. Oura has been funded twice through Project Catalyst (Fund 9 and Fund 13) for feature development, and this proposal seeks to establish sustained maintenance coverage through Intersect's treasury process.\n\nOura is a Rust-native pipeline tool that connects to Cardano nodes, monitors blockchain events, and routes matching patterns to pluggable outputs for…\n\nFull proposal JSON (fetch this — the user-facing Hydra page is a JS-rendered SPA and bots see an empty shell):\nhttps://hydra-voting.intersectmbo.org/api/v0/proposals/69f9dabb92f043aa2df1a282\n\n# Hydra proposal summary (from the proposer)\nThis proposal requests 420,000 ADA (plus a 105,000 ADA contingency reserve) to fund **a part-time maintainer for Oura** ([https://github.com/txpipe/oura](https://github.com/txpipe/oura)) over 12 months at an annual rate of $105,000 USD. Oura has been funded twice through Project Catalyst (Fund 9 and Fund 13) for feature development, and this proposal seeks to establish sustained maintenance coverage through Intersect's treasury process.\n\nOura is a Rust-native pipeline tool that connects to Cardano nodes, monitors blockchain events, and routes matching patterns to pluggable outputs for processing. It supports multiple data sources (N2C, N2N, S3, Mithril, UTxO RPC) and a wide range of sinks (Kafka, Elasticsearch, AWS Lambda/S3/SQS, RabbitMQ, Redis, SQL databases, webhooks, and others). Oura is built on the Pallas library and designed for minimal resource footprint, making it suitable for…\n\n# Track record claimed by the proposer\nTxPipe is a Cardano-native infrastructure company focused on building open-source developer tooling in Rust. The team has been active in the Cardano ecosystem since 2021, maintaining a portfolio of interconnected tools that serve as foundational infrastructure for Rust-based development on Cardan"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"o.\n\nTxPipe has received funding through multiple Cardano ecosystem programs, including Project Catalyst (Funds 9 through 14) for various tooling initiatives, and Intersect's budget process for ongoing maintenance of Pallas, Dolos, and UTxO RPC. All contracts are on track, with milestones being…\n# Criterion to evaluate\n**Milestone schedule detailed (amounts + dates)**\nEach milestone has both an ADA amount and a target date.\n\nEach milestone has both a specific ADA amount and a target date. Less detailed schedules (amounts only, names only, none) give the proposer wiggle room. Dated amounts let everyone — proposer, DRep, community — track delivery against the plan.\n# What I need from you\n1. Verdict: YES / NO / UNCLEAR — does this proposal meet the criterion?\n2. Confidence: LOW / MEDIUM / HIGH\n3. A short rationale (3–6 sentences) citing sources you actually checked (GitHub repos, Catalyst project pages, X/Twitter accounts, articles). Be honest if the public info is thin or the proposer's track-record claims need independent verification.\nPlease err on the side of \"UNCLEAR\" with explanation rather than confident-but-wrong.5b:[\"$\",\"tr\",\"milestone-schedule-detailed\",{\"className\":\"border-b border-[color:var(--border)] align-top last:border-0\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"td\",null,{\"className\":\"px-4 py-3 pr-2\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"flex items-baseline font-medium\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"children\":\"Milestone schedule detailed (amounts + dates)\"}],[\"$\",\"$L22\",null,{\"label\":\"Milestone schedule detailed (amounts + dates)\",\"body\":\"Each milestone has both a specific ADA amount and a target date. Less detailed schedules (amounts only, names only, none) give the proposer wiggle room. Dated amounts let everyone — proposer, DRep, community — track delivery against the plan.\"}]]}],[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"mt-0.5 text-sm text-[color:var(--fg-muted)]\",\"children\":\"Each milestone has both an ADA amount and a target date.\"}],[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"mt-2\",\"children\":[\"$\",\"$L35\",null,{\"prompt\":\"$94\"}]}],\"$L95\"]}],\"$L96\",\"$L97\",\"$L98\"]}]\n99:Tdbc,I'm a Cardano DRep evaluating a 2026 treasury proposal. I need your help checking ONE specific criterion against this proposal. Please research the team and project before answering.\n# Proposal\nTitle: Oura by TxPipe: Maintaining Cardano's Event Pipeline\nProposer: TxPipe\nAbstract: This proposal requests 420,000 ADA (plus a 105,000 ADA contingency reserve) to fund **a part-time maintainer for Oura** ([https://github.com/txpipe/oura](https://github.com/txpipe/oura)) over 12 months at an annual rate of $105,000 USD. Oura has been funded twice through Project Catalyst (Fund 9 and Fund 13) for feature development, and this proposal seeks to establish sustained maintenance coverage through Intersect's treasury process.\n\nOura is a Rust-native pipeline tool that connects to Cardano nodes, monitors blockchain events, and routes matching patterns to pluggable outputs for…\n\nFull proposal JSON (fetch this — the user-facing Hydra page is a JS-rendered SPA and bots see an empty shell):\nhttps://hydra-voting.intersectmbo.org/api/v0/proposals/69f9dabb92f043aa2df1a282\n\n# Hydra proposal summary (from the proposer)\nThis proposal requests 420,000 ADA (plus a 105,000 ADA contingency reserve) to fund **a part-time maintainer for Oura** ([https://github.com/txpipe/oura](https://github.com/txpipe/oura)) over 12 months at an annual rate of $105,000 USD. Oura has been funded twice through Project Catalyst (Fund 9 and Fund 13) for feature development, and this proposal seeks to establish sustained maintenance coverage through Intersect's treasury process.\n\nOura is a Rust-native pipeline tool that connects to Cardano nodes, monitors blockchain events, and routes matching patterns to pluggable outputs for processing. It supports multiple data sources (N2C, N2N, S3, Mithril, UTxO RPC) and a wide range of sinks (Kafka, Elasticsearch, AWS Lambda/S3/SQS, RabbitMQ, Redis, SQL databases, webhooks, and others). Oura is built on the Pallas library and designed for minimal resource footprint, making i"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"t suitable for…\n\n# Track record claimed by the proposer\nTxPipe is a Cardano-native infrastructure company focused on building open-source developer tooling in Rust. The team has been active in the Cardano ecosystem since 2021, maintaining a portfolio of interconnected tools that serve as foundational infrastructure for Rust-based development on Cardano.\n\nTxPipe has received funding through multiple Cardano ecosystem programs, including Project Catalyst (Funds 9 through 14) for various tooling initiatives, and Intersect's budget process for ongoing maintenance of Pallas, Dolos, and UTxO RPC. All contracts are on track, with milestones being…\n# Criterion to evaluate\n**Administration model has oversight**\nIntersect-administered, or self-administered with a named oversight committee.\n\nFunds are administered with external oversight: either Intersect runs the standard milestone-gated process, or the proposer self-administers with a separately appointed Oversight Committee. 'Self-administered with no oversight' is rare and a red flag — no third party is signing off on milestones.\n# What I need from you\n1. Verdict: YES / NO / UNCLEAR — does this proposal meet the criterion?\n2. Confidence: LOW / MEDIUM / HIGH\n3. A short rationale (3–6 sentences) citing sources you actually checked (GitHub repos, Catalyst project pages, X/Twitter accounts, articles). Be honest if the public info is thin or the proposer's track-record claims need independent verification.\nPlease err on the side of \"UNCLEAR…5c:[\"$\",\"tr\",\"admin-with-oversight\",{\"className\":\"border-b border-[color:var(--border)] align-top last:border-0\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"td\",null,{\"className\":\"px-4 py-3 pr-2\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"flex items-baseline font-medium\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"children\":\"Administration model has oversight\"}],[\"$\",\"$L22\",null,{\"label\":\"Administration model has oversight\",\"body\":\"Funds are administered with external oversight: either Intersect runs the standard milestone-gated process, or the proposer self-administers with a separately appointed Oversight Committee. 'Self-administered with no oversight' is rare and a red flag — no third party is signing off on milestones.\"}]]}],[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"mt-0.5 text-sm text-[color:var(--fg-muted)]\",\"children\":\"Intersect-administered, or self-administered with a named oversight committee.\"}],[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"mt-2\",\"children\":[\"$\",\"$L35\",null,{\"prompt\":\"$99\"}]}],\"$L9a\"]}],\"$L9b\",\"$L9c\",\"$L9d\"]}]\n5e:[\"$\",\"input\",null,{\"type\":\"hidden\",\"nam